{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB11576 - MONDO_1356",
  "verbalization": "Ferric Oxide is strongly associated with Iron Deficiency Anemia through a series of indirect pathways. The drug is linked to Hypochromic Anemia and Microcytic Anemia, both of which are hallmark features of Iron Deficiency Anemia. These anemias are further connected to Ferrous Gluconate, a common treatment for iron deficiency, which in turn is indicated to treat Iron Deficiency Anemia. The evidence suggests that Ferric Oxide may influence the body's iron metabolism, potentially leading to the development of iron deficiency. The mechanism is supported by the shared indication of Ferrous Gluconate with Iron Deficiency Anemia, implying a possible role in iron homeostasis. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential link between Ferric Oxide and the pathophysiology of Iron Deficiency Anemia, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
